pper/DocumentParser.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":10832,"endPos":11033,"startLine":247,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":250,"endLineOffset":5,"length":202}]}]},{"comment":"The removal of the `indexSettings().getSkipIgnoredSourceWrite()` check from both `markFieldAsCopyTo` and `canAddIgnoredField` is a behavioral change: indices that previously opted out of writing ignored source will now write it unconditionally (for synthetic source). If this setting is being intentionally retired, that\u0027s fine, but it\u0027s worth confirming that no downstream code or user-facing documentation still references it, and that the removal is covered by a migration/deprecation note.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DocumentParserContext.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DocumentParserContext.java-12348:12437-14604:14637","promptId":"#3DY0Q","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DocumentParserContext.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DocumentParserContext.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":12348,"endPos":12437,"startLine":370,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":370,"endLineOffset":101,"length":90}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":14604,"endPos":14637,"startLine":420,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":420,"endLineOffset":45,"length":34}]},{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DocumentParserContext.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DocumentParserContext.java--13573:13633","promptId":"#GX4Z0","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DocumentParserContext.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DocumentParserContext.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":13573,"endPos":13633,"startLine":386,"startLineOffset":15,"endLine":386,"endLineOffset":75,"length":61}]}]},{"comment":"Two concerns:\n1. A full `RootDocumentParserContext` is constructed (allocating a `LuceneDocument`, computing nested-doc limits, etc.) solely to obtain a parser for `parseDocForMissingValues`, which only calls `context.parser()`. Passing the `XContentParser` directly (or a lighter wrapper) would avoid the unnecessary allocation.\n2. This second pass re-parses the entire document source. For large documents with only one or two missing-value fields, this is a non-trivial cost incurred on every index operation. Consider whether the `parentNames` skip optimization is sufficient, or whether a more targeted extraction (e.g., using the original parser\u0027s position recorded during the first pass) would be preferable.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DocumentParser.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DocumentParser.java--7092:8104","promptId":"#G15RZ","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DocumentParser.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DocumentParser.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":7092,"endPos":8104,"startLine":162,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":186,"endLineOffset":5,"length":1013}]}]},{"comment":"The `parseDocForMissingValues` method has a path-tracking issue:\nThe `path` list is only appended to when a `START_OBJECT`/`START_ARRAY` is encountered with a non-null `fieldName`, but it is unconditionally popped on every `END_OBJECT`/`END_ARRAY`. For objects that are *elements of an array* (which have no field name), the corresponding `END_OBJECT` still pops the path, corrupting it for subsequent siblings. For example, given `{\"arr\": [{\"x\":1}, {\"target\": 2}]}` with target `\"arr.target\"`, after the first element\u0027s `END_OBJECT` the path is incorrectly emptied, so `\"target\"` in the second element resolves to `\"target\"` instead of `\"arr.target\"`.\nIn the current call sites the target is always resolved at the `FIELD_NAME` level (encoding the next token as the whole structure), so this latent bug is not triggered today. However, the method is general-purpose and would silently fail if a future use case requires locating a leaf *inside* a later array element.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DocumentParser.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DocumentParser.java--8110:10826","promptId":"#BDPYD","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DocumentParser.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DocumentParser.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":8110,"endPos":10826,"startLine":188,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":245,"endLineOffset":5,"length":2717}]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":164,"line":164,"comment_lines":["[][164]"],"review_comment":["This would also be empty incase synthetic source isn\u0027t used?","Correct, lemme assert."],"path":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DocumentParser.java","id":36822,"created_at":"2024-09-18T07:22:53Z","original_position":51,"side":"RIGHT","position":51,"submitted_on_commit":"430f0645b6b9fa5bcf3f01f3708775e11d73cc83","diff_hunk":"@@ -155,6 +159,122 @@ private static void internalParseDocument(MetadataFieldMapper[] metadataFieldsMa\n         }\n     }\n \n+    private void addIgnoredSourceMissingValues(DocumentParserContext context) throws IOException {\n+        Collection\u003cIgnoredSourceFieldMapper.NameValue\u003e ignoredFieldsMissingValues \u003d context.getIgnoredFieldsMissingValues();\n+        if (ignoredFieldsMissingValues.isEmpty()) {","submitted_line":164},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"Two concerns:\n1. A full `RootDocumentParserContext` is constructed (allocating a `LuceneDocument`, computing nested-doc limits, etc.) solely to obtain a parser for `parseDocForMissingValues`, which only calls `context.parser()`. Passing the `XContentParser` directly (or a lighter wrapper) would avoid the unnecessary allocation.\n2. This second pass re-parses the entire document source. For large documents with only one or two missing-value fields, this is a non-trivial cost incurred on every index operation. Consider whether the `parentNames` skip optimization is sufficient, or whether a more targeted extraction (e.g., using the original parser\u0027s position recorded during the first pass) would be preferable.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DocumentParser.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DocumentParser.java--7092:8104","promptId":"#G15RZ","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DocumentParser.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DocumentParser.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":7092,"endPos":8104,"startLine":162,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":186,"endLineOffset":5,"length":1013}]}]}]}],"coveredGroundTruth":1,"uncoveredGroundTruth":0,"coveredMatchable":33,"uncoveredMatchable":1,"timing":311954,"tokensIn":16218,"tokensOut":17951}